Mukund,

Quick thought before we lock in levothyroxine: I noted in the lab report
that the sample was drawn ~35 min after breakfast. TSH can be 30-40%
suppressed (or in some cases falsely elevated) in non-fasting states.
Before committing to a 6-8 week trial, can we repeat the panel in true
fasting state? The patient's symptoms (fatigue, mild weight gain) are
non-specific enough that a couple of weeks delay is acceptable.

If the fasting recheck still shows TSH >5, then yes, levothyroxine 25
mcg trial. Otherwise let's avoid medicalizing a likely-spurious result.

I'll send the patient a reminder to come in fasting on 16-Apr.

— Suresh

